{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f50ca7ec9196bfe9","name":"Dual Weapon Mastery I","source":{"id":"source:reference-f50ca7ec9196bfe9","title":"Dual Weapon Mastery I","revision":24945,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T15:53:58Z","sha256":"5f2689a8ae03843529d51bf7a7140e14040888fe2dda86ea75a455824ccfc9ee","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24945","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Dual%20Weapon%20Mastery%20I&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f50ca7ec9196bfe9","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["You are adept at fighting with two weapons and double weapons.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," 13, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," +1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Effect:"]}," When you attack with two weapons, or with both ends of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Weapon"}," as part of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full_Attack"}," Action, you take a -5 penalty (instead of a -10 penalty) on all attack rolls until the start of your next turn. You only gain this reduced penalty if you are wielding a weapon with which you are proficient. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Weapons"}," cannot be used in one hand, so this feat has no effect on them.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Normal:"]}," If you use a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full_Attack"}," Action to make more than one attack on your turn, you take a -10 penalty on all attack rolls for the round.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Combined Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Combined_Feat"},":"]}," If you have the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Quick Draw"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Quick_Draw","referenceId":"reference:ad3a4bd9344ce557"}," feat, you can draw or holster two weapons with a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},"; you must have both hands free to draw both weapons, and each weapon must be able to be held in one hand.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," I'm curious as to the perceived balance factor of Dual Weapon Mastery versus ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"},". Dual Weapon Mastery I is available sooner, and you can offset its penalties by taking more ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"}," works for only one type of weapon, and you can reduce its penalties only with Prestige Class ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"},". Since both grant an extra attack, why would you want ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"},"?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," The balancing factor is that Dual Weapon Mastery works only with ",{"tag":"a","children":["One-Handed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/One-Handed"}," weapons (that is, weapons that do less damage), but ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"},"/",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"}," works with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Two-Handed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Two-Handed"}," weapons (but only one type of them). For example:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["A Dual Weapon Mastery specialist might use two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Blaster Pistols"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Blaster_Pistols"},", which deal 3d8 points of damage per weapon, or a potential of 6d8 points from both."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"}," specialist might use a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Blaster Rifle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Blaster_Rifle","referenceId":"reference:40670bfa52c77cbd"},", which deals 3d10 points of damage but has a much better ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"},". In addition, the weapon is capable of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Autofire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Autofire"},", so it can deal up to 5d10 points of damage with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst_Fire","referenceId":"reference:ff3da4756d0ccd5c"},"."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["This also means that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"}," can be used with much larger weapons, such as those on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},", while a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," would have no particular reason to use Dual Weapon Mastery because such weapons can't be operated with one hand.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Finally, don't forget that someone can use both Dual Weapon Mastery and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"},"/",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"},". So even if Dual Weapon Mastery appears more attractive at first, you might want to take ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double_Attack","referenceId":"reference:73f4a3f279861109"},"/",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"}," later.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
